STATUS   ID       SEVERITY  CONTROL
FAIL     SSH-002  high      Password authentication disabled
         passwordauthentication is yes, expected no
         Passwords can be guessed or reused from leaks; SSH keys cannot be
         brute-forced.
         fix: not automated yet
FAIL     FW-001   medium    Incoming traffic denied by default
         no firewall rules filter incoming traffic
         Without it, any service listening on all addresses, such as a database
         left at its defaults, is reachable from the internet. A firewall at
         your provider also protects the server, but this check cannot see it.
         fix: not automated yet
FAIL     SSH-001  medium    Root login disabled
         permitrootlogin is without-password, expected no
         Root is the one account name every scanner tries, and its actions are
         not tied to a person. Log in as a named user and use sudo.
         fix: not automated yet
FAIL     UPD-001  medium    Security updates installed automatically
         unattended-upgrades is not installed;
         APT::Periodic::Update-Package-Lists is not set;
         APT::Periodic::Unattended-Upgrade is not set
         Attackers scan for a flaw soon after its fix is published. Unattended
         upgrades install security fixes on their own, so a server nobody logs
         into still gets them.
         fix: sudo vps-ready apply --module updates.auto
FAIL     SSH-005  low       X11 forwarding disabled
         x11forwarding is yes, expected no
         A server has no use for graphical apps, and a forwarded display lets
         the server reach into your desktop session.
         fix: not automated yet

